Modifications
-------------
Operon's fork discipline is that upstream is changed as little as possible: the
whole point of building on Kaneo is to keep Kaneo's feature set — boards,
backlog, labels, time tracking, webhooks, search and the MCP server — exactly as
upstream built it. Only four kinds of change are permitted, and every file this
fork touches is declared in Operon's `docs/fork-discipline.md`:

  1. Auth wiring — Operon is the OpenID Connect provider; Kaneo's own local
     sign-in is disabled by environment, and the post-login hook reports the new
     Kaneo user back to Operon.
  2. Branding and chrome — the product is called Initiative inside Operon, and
     the sidebar carries Operon's surface switcher.
  3. A `telegraph` integration type with an authorised external-link write
     route, so a Kaneo task can carry the Nostr event id of the chat message it
     came from.
  4. Workspace bootstrap — a single shared workspace, created by the first
     admin's login and joined by everyone after.

Changes landed on this branch so far:

